rainers  supported by a command and control  element at a military base in south east  england  the first cohort  of caf personnel will depart from  edmonton alberta starting next week  [Music]  [Music]  indeed general heir shared that when he  met last week with the  commander-in-chief of the armed forces  of ukraine general zoluzni reiterated  how much ukrainians valued canada's  powerful training mission  i have also been in touch with defense  minister reznikov including today  who thanked me  for canada's continued support for  ukraine's security  sovereignty and  stability  on behalf of canada i want to thank the  united kingdom and my counterpart  secretary wallace for leading this  initiative and for providing the  facilities needed to resume training i  also salute the remarkable courage and  bravery of the armed forces of ukraine  in these most difficult circumstances  moving now to update on military aid to  ukraine  our commitment to ukraine and two  canadians watching this at home  is that we will continue to provide  ukraine not only with the skills to  defend their country  but also with the equipment necessary to  do so  through our own stocks and inventory we  have provided anti-tank weapon systems  and ammunition  hand grenades m triple sevens artillery  guns and small arms to ukraine over the  last number of months  to bolster ukraine's defense we have  also been procuring military aid through  canadian industry including 56 drone  cameras eight rochelle armored vehicles  demining equipment  and satellite imagery  in addition  at the nato's leader summit the prime  minister and i announced that canada was  working to finalize an agreement with  gdls to supply 39 armored combat support  vehicles  and today  i am pleased to confirm that an  agreement has been achieved with the  company and that these vehicles will be  delivered  straight off the assembly line to  address some of ukraine's most pressing  battlefield needs  the company has informed us that the  deliveries to europe of the first  vehicles will begin in the coming weeks  working in close partnership with the  ukrainian armed forces and with defence  minister resnikoff we are also equipping  these vehicles with additional  modern state-of-the-art armor and  machine guns as well as ammunition for  these machine guns  moving now to cooperation with our  allies  our canadian armed forces have also  helped our nato allies deliver over 3  million  pounds of military aid and military  equipment  from our allies since february in  support of ukraine and we continue  to work with domestic partners to  identify specific defense industry  niches where canada has a competitive  advantage that could continue supporting  ukraine  in the long term  canada  says  [Music]  in short canada is taking an all hands  on deck approach  in our support for ukraine and in  defense of the rules-based international  order our support will not waver  in conclusion  our adversaries are watching us closely  eager to see cracks in our solidarity  hoping for signs of disunity  and they may think that the nato  alliance can be divided  but we are more united than ever in our  support of ukraine  the resumption of operation unifier  is just one more example of this support  thank you  merci  i'm happy to take your questions  thank you merci please press star one at  this time if you have a question  the first question is from liberty the  canadian press please go ahead  yes thank you minister um i wanted to  ask about the um  sorry the uh  i lost my train of thought there um just  about the the deployment and obviously  the canadian forces is uh very stretched  now we have a number of commitments all  over the place we've also seen what's  happening in china and i'm just  wondering about the state of the forces  in terms of uh its ability to uh to  provide such a large commitment and and  also kind of on the flip side why it's  only for four months  thank you for the question lee  