ing  system at the current time but we are  monitoring the developments  and we will leave no stone unturned in  our work to ensure the safe delivery and  the use of military aid  next question questions  thank you  that guest stands for about the next  question is from kevin gallagher ctv  national news please go ahead  morning minister thanks for taking our  questions uh ukraine's ambassador to  canada is expected to again express  disappointment from ukraine about  canada's decision to waive the  sanctions on the turbines um so i guess  like my question to you is uh although  ukraine has been asking for canada to  trade its troops it's also disappointed  about canada indirectly helping russia  fund this war so what do you say to your  ukrainian allies today  um you know about this kind of  disconnect and um  i guess solidarity  well i'd like to start off by saying  kevin that i have been in touch with  minister resnikoff this morning and we  continue to stand in solidarity with  ukraine  and  with our current counterparts in the  ukrainian government  and they recognize that we stand with  ukraine shoulder to shoulder full stop  we will continue to impose severe costs  on the russian regime in response to  putin's illegal and unprovoked war  against ukraine  at the same time it is important for us  to support our  european friends and allies as they work  to end their dependency on russian gas  imports as quickly as possible canada is  going to continue to work to stabilize  energy markets and to develop long-term  and sustainable solutions on energy  supplies  back to the training mission in uk um  how long is it going to last and how  many ukrainian soldiers will this train  i guess maybe to specify  no foreign  nationals will be trained is only  ukrainian nationals for being trained at  this camp by uk and  canadian servicemen  and women this training mission is for  ukrainian military new recruits  and canada's contribution is going  to be  extensive  up to  