ection of ukraine  and in support of the international  rules-based order which has kept us all  safe since the end of the second world  war  when it comes to timing ukraine's  government has repeatedly pushed for  canada to restart the training in a  third country why not do this earlier  what has changed now  actually the reality is that we have  been very consistent  in  offering whatever support we can from a  military perspective  to ukraine let me give you a  another example  when we donated the m triple sevens  we also began training  ukrainian  forces on the use of the m7777s in the  third country  and our  niche  area of expertise in training is well  recognized around the world jen  stoltenberg for example has repeatedly  mentioned it to me and publicly how  important canada's role has been in  training  so i see this as a continuum  in fact of various types of aid that  canada is putting on the table be it  from caf inventory be it from  procurements from canadian industry in  areas of expertise such as cameras for  drones or in armored vehicles and now be  it from large-scale training missions  which we clearly have expertise in doing  and which the canadian armed forces are  very much looking forward to  participating in  [Music]  foreign  and  um  [Music]  foreign  uh  um  foreign  uh  [Music]  [Music]  and we'll take another question  please thank you merci la questions  vivant the next question is from david  paglice the ottawa citizen please go  ahead  hey thank you um canada has been in the  discussions with south korea over the  purchase of a potential purchase of a  hundred thousand uh  rounds of artillery ammunition um i was  wondering uh where you're at with that  and uh if that deal is going to be  signed and sealed so the ammunition  could be sent to ukraine  i'll begin by saying that  perhaps as is evidenced uh today from my  remarks  already that we are  continuing  to put whatever we can on the table for  ukraine whether it's from  the inventory and stocks of the canadian  armed forces whether it is through our  relationships and requests of canadian  industry which they have very much risen  to assist us with  or whether it is coordinating with our  allies through the  defense contact group for example which  has been set up by  secretary austin of the united states so  we are very comprehensive in the work  that we are doing in terms of military  aid and equipment for ukraine  on the specific subject of additional  procurements  we are certainly  in communication with a number of  suppliers  we  are also in touch with minister  resnikoff  to identify what ukraine's immediate and  most pressing needs are  and i want to say that our  contributions of military aid have  directly lined up  with the specific requests  that minister resnickoff has made of me  directly and us as a country  and we will continue  to  do whatever we can to stand shoulder to  shoulder with ukraine and as i said we  are in touch with multiple suppliers in  that vein  and follow-up question please  so are you going to proceed with the  south south korean deal uh yes or no  actually it would be imprudent for me to  announce any transaction before it is  finalized it is not my style and i will  make sure that i have all the teas  crossed and eyes dotted before anything  is announced and that includes  the question that you are posing to me  right now  thank you and one final question  thank you merci  the last question  um  officials are a lot more concerned about  ukraine's leadership than they are  letting on and there is deep mistrust  between the white house and president  zielinski of ukraine  it  [Music]  now  is  don't know  [Music]  [Music]  zealand for example  [Music]  continue  [Music]  thank you everyone for joining us today  this concludes today's press conference  merci beaucoup thank you  thank you merci the conference has now  ended the  cafe  please disconnect your lines at this  time very similar crochet button

